{"id":"119-s-3627","label":"S. 3627","congress":119,"title":"Pregnant Students’ Rights Act","latestVote":"2026-01-27","rollIds":["Senate:2:12"],"hasMetadata":true,"chambers":["Senate"],"congressUrl":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/senate-bill/3627","metadataUrl":"https://www.govinfo.gov/bulkdata/BILLSTATUS/119/s/BILLSTATUS-119s3627.xml","metadata":{"title":"Pregnant Students’ Rights Act","introduced":"2026-01-13","latestAction":"Cloture on the motion to proceed to the measure not invoked in Senate by Yea-Nay Vote. 47 - 45. Record Vote Number: 12. (CR S286)","latestActionDate":"2026-01-27","policyArea":"Education","subjects":["Abortion","Higher education","School administration","Sex and reproductive health","Women's education","Women's health"],"sponsors":["Sen. Moody, Ashley [R-FL]"],"cosponsors":["Sen. Blackburn, Marsha [R-TN]","Sen. Budd, Ted [R-NC]","Sen. Hyde-Smith, Cindy [R-MS]","Sen. Lankford, James [R-OK]","Sen. Cassidy, Bill [R-LA]","Sen. Banks, Jim [R-IN]","Sen. Daines, Steve [R-MT]","Sen. Scott, Rick [R-FL]","Sen. Grassley, Chuck [R-IA]","Sen. Wicker, Roger F. [R-MS]","Sen. Thune, John [R-SD]","Sen. Mullin, Markwayne [R-OK]","Sen. Cruz, Ted [R-TX]","Sen. Justice, James C. [R-WV]","Sen. Husted, Jon [R-OH]","Sen. Cornyn, John [R-TX]","Sen. McCormick, David [R-PA]","Sen. Graham, Lindsey [R-SC]","Sen. Lee, Mike [R-UT]","Sen. Lummis, Cynthia M. [R-WY]","Sen. Scott, Tim [R-SC]","Sen. Marshall, Roger [R-KS]","Sen. Moreno, Bernie [R-OH]","Sen. Graham, Darline [R-SC]"],"committees":[],"laws":[],"committeeReports":[],"costEstimates":[],"relatedBills":[{"title":"Pregnant Students’ Rights Act","relationship":"Related bill","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/6359"}],"textVersions":[{"date":"2026-01-14","stage":"Placed on Calendar Senate","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/BILLS-119s3627pcs/xml/BILLS-119s3627pcs.xml"}],"summaries":[{"date":"2026-01-13","stage":"Introduced in Senate","text":"Pregnant Students' Rights Act\n\n This bill requires each institution of higher education (IHE) that participates in federal student aid programs to provide certain information to prospective and enrolled students on the rights and resources for pregnant students to carry a baby to term or students who may become pregnant while enrolled at the IHE to carry a baby to term.\n\n In particular, this required information must include\n\n  \na list of community and on-campus resources that exist to help a pregnant student in carrying the baby to term and caring for the baby after birth,  \ninformation about the accommodations available to help a pregnant student carry the baby to term and parent the baby after birth, and \ninformation on how to file a discrimination complaint related to the student's determination to carry a baby to term."}],"actions":[{"date":"2026-01-27","text":"Cloture on the motion to proceed to the measure not invoked in Senate by Yea-Nay Vote. 47 - 45. Record Vote Number: 12. (CR S286)"},{"date":"2026-01-15","text":"Cloture motion on the motion to proceed presented in Senate. (CR S262)"},{"date":"2026-01-15","text":"Motion to proceed to consideration of measure made in Senate. (consideration: CR S262)"},{"date":"2026-01-14","text":"Read the second time. Placed on Senate Legislative Calendar under General Orders. Calendar No. 300."},{"date":"2026-01-13","text":"Introduced in the Senate. Read the first time. Placed on Senate Legislative Calendar under Read the First Time."},{"date":"2026-01-13","text":"Introduced in Senate"}]},"votes":[{"chamber":"Senate","congress":119,"session":2,"roll":12,"date":"2026-01-27","time":"05:26 PM","question":"On Cloture on the Motion to Proceed S. 3627","description":"Motion to Invoke Cloture on the Motion to Proceed to S. 3627","result":"Cloture on the Motion to Proceed Rejected (47-45, 3/5 majority required)","amendment":"","amendmentDetail":"","tieBreaker":"","url":"https://www.senate.gov/legislative/LIS/roll_call_votes/vote1192/vote_119_2_00012